 3. 🥕 New Dem push for MAHA voters 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Lindsey Bailey/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Some Democrats are courting the "Make America Healthy Again" base, hoping pitches on food safety and environmental health will attract voters disillusioned with the Trump administration's lack of progress, Axios' Caitlin Owens writes. 

 Why it matters: Policies around cleaning up the food supply and agricultural practices helped forge a coalition that's credited with helping President Trump win a second term. Some Democrats say they're better positioned to take on established interests through regulation and are honing messaging ahead of the 2028 presidential race.

 The Center for American Progress, a progressive think tank, recently released a proposal focused on healthier foods and reducing harmful chemicals alongside polling showing Democrats are poised to claim the agenda as their own. 🔬 Zoom in: Michigan Senate candidate Abdul El-Sayed last month released a proposal titled "Building a Healthier America" that included calls for banning certain pesticides — a key unrealized MAHA goal — and healthier school meals.

 House Democrats' health care working group included a section in its policy agenda called "Reclaiming MAHA and Protecting American Families." Keep reading ... Get Axios Future of Health Care . 

 
 
