 4. 📈 Charted: AI&#x27;s price plunge 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Ramp. Chart: Axios/Matt Phillips The price companies pay for AI tokens has plunged roughly 35% since the end of June, Axios' Matt Phillips writes from Ramp's AI price index. 

 Why it matters: Falling prices for tokens — a basic unit of AI usage — raise questions about the strength of demand for AI and how much revenue the data center boom will ultimately generate for investors. Get Axios Markets . 

 
 
