 5. 🇧🇷 Trump opens door for Bolsonaro 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Flávio Bolsonaro speaks Sunday in Brasília, Brazil, after the presidential runoff. Photo: Eraldo Peres/AP The U.S. government is granting visas to Flávio Bolsonaro and his family following his defeat in Brazil's presidential election, a senior Trump administration official tells Axios' Marc Caputo and Rebecca Falconer. 

 Why it matters: The move comes days after Brazilian President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva defeated Bolsonaro, the son of former President Jair Bolsonaro. Following the election, Brazil's Supreme Court ordered Bolsonaro to surrender his passports and barred him from leaving the country.

 The order stems from an ongoing investigation into alleged money laundering. Bolsonaro has denied wrongdoing. 🔭 Zoom out: President Trump and his administration have repeatedly backed the Bolsonaro family, with the president denouncing the prosecution of the elder Bolsonaro as a "witch hunt."

 Trump suggested Brazil's election was "rigged." Keep reading . 

 
 
