 8. 🎃 1 fun thing: Pumpkin Picasso 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Farmer Mike Valladao carves a pumpkin at the Safeway World Championship Pumpkin Weigh-Off in Half Moon Bay, Calif., this month. Photo: Jeff Chiu/AP Mike Valladao — a systems engineer at a cybersecurity company in the Bay Area — has spent four decades moonlighting as "Farmer Mike," the "Picasso of Pumpkin Carvers."

 He's sculpted hundreds of gourds into ghoulish faces, seaside landscapes, witches, dragons and pop culture figures like Yoda and Charlie Brown. Valladao uses Atlantic pumpkins weighing 100 to 1,000 pounds. They have thick skins that allow him to cut protruding facial features shallow or deep.

 The photo above shows Valladao carving at this month's 53rd Safeway World Championship Pumpkin Weigh-Off in Half Moon Bay, Calif., where his family opened the first feed and seed store in the 19th century. Go deeper . 

 
 
